### Secrets / local config ###
# ONLY the files that hold real credentials are ignored.
#
# Previously application.properties was ignored too, which meant a fresh clone had NO
# configuration at all — no port, no active profile, no CORS list — and could not be
# started or deployed. Configuration everyone needs belongs in git; only the secrets do
# not. So these two stay out:
src/main/resources/application.properties
src/main/resources/application-dev.properties
src/main/resources/application-prod.properties
src/main/resources/application-local.properties
#
# …and these ARE tracked, because they contain only ${ENV_VAR} placeholders and
# comments, never a credential:
#   application.properties                  (base config, local defaults)
#   application-prod.properties             (production, env vars with no fallbacks)
#   application-dev.properties.example      (template to copy for local development)
